.bd
NAME
.in +5
.br
.bd
xargs
- run a command with arguments read from stdin
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
SYNTAX
.in +5
.br
.bd
xargs command [argument ...]
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
DESCRIPTION
.in +5
.br
Xargs reads words from its standard input and runs
.bd
command
with those words as arguments, in batches small enough for the shell
to exec.  It is how a
.bd
find
pipeline removes any number of files without tripping the shell's
"too many arguments":
.sp
.ti +5
.bd
find . -name '*.o' -print | xargs rm -f
.sp
If
.bd
command
has no slash in its name, it is looked for in
.bd
. ,
.bd
/bin
and
.bd
/usr/bin ,
the way the shell does.
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
SEE ALSO
.in +5
.br
find (1), rm (1)
